From da4d2564aa9d89faccef55be3923b08ca64eb06c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 04:21:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MFront: stress of the initialize functions exported for all
 stress measures

For finite strain behaviours, the stress computed by an initialize
function was only exported for the Cauchy stress of standard finite
strain behaviours. For the other stress measures, and for the behaviours
written in the Green-Lagrange or the logarithmic strain, the stress was
written in a local array and lost. It is now converted to the stress
measure of the caller, with the deformation gradient at the beginning of
the time step, which is the state used by initialize functions.

The conversion of the Cauchy stress to the stress measure of the caller
is moved to MFront/GenericBehaviour/StressMeasures.hxx, shared by the
three drivers.

Tests: initialize function of SaintVenantKirchhoffElasticity with the
second and first Piola-Kirchhoff stresses.
---
 mfront/include/CMakeLists.txt                 |  1 +
 .../GreenLagrangeStrainIntegrate.hxx          | 21 +++++-
 .../LogarithmicStrainIntegrate.hxx            | 15 +++-
 ...StandardFiniteStrainBehaviourIntegrate.hxx | 71 +++++++------------
 .../GenericBehaviour/StressMeasures.hxx       | 57 +++++++++++++++
 .../generic-parallel/compare-all.sh           |  6 ++
 6 files changed, 123 insertions(+), 48 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 mfront/include/MFront/GenericBehaviour/StressMeasures.hxx

